---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { profile } from '../data/site';
import { sitePath } from '../utils/paths';
---

<Base
  title="About | James Young"
  description="About James Young, a senior applied machine-learning and data-science leader working across biological discovery, scientific ML, and operational decision systems."
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <span class="page-path">ForetoData / about</span>
      <h1>Biological understanding, machine learning, and operational decisions.</h1>
      <div class="page-intro">
        <span class="section-kicker">About James</span>
        <p>The difficult part is defining the right problem, experiment, or decision before choosing a model.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell two-column">
      <article class="editorial">
        <p class="lead-paragraph">I am a senior applied machine-learning and data-science leader with a PhD in Biological Sciences, specializing in molecular biology. I work across scientific questions, analytical systems, and the decisions those systems are meant to improve.</p>

        <h2>Scientific depth</h2>
        <p>My research centers on machine-learning-guided functional discovery and engineering in undercharacterized microbial systems. Oxygen-tolerant nitrogen fixation is a flagship application, connecting comparative genomics, condition-specific multi-omics, protein representation, candidate prioritization, and validation planning.</p>

        <h2>Operational judgment</h2>
        <p>Industry work has involved causal inference, forecasting, targeting, resource allocation, and analytical implementation. That experience shapes how I think about scientific ML: models have to fit the decision, expose their assumptions, survive operating constraints, and support measurement after adoption.</p>

        <h2>Translation</h2>
        <p>Much of my work is translation: keeping biological context visible in model design, explaining uncertainty to decision-makers, and tying analytical output to experiments or operating choices.</p>

        <div class="text-links">
          <a class="text-link" href={profile.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <a class="text-link" href={sitePath('work')}>Selected work <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <aside>
        <div class="quiet-panel">
          <span class="meta-label">Compact profile</span>
          <ul class="question-list">
            <li>Computational biology and scientific machine learning</li>
            <li>Protein and gene-function discovery</li>
            <li>Comparative genomics and multi-omic analysis</li>
            <li>Protein language models and active learning</li>
            <li>Causal inference, forecasting, and resource allocation</li>
            <li>Operational decision systems</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
